From 31d813a3b8cbde2d09ba4dee282ca29096541006 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andreas Hindborg <a.hindborg@kernel.org>
Date: Fri, 20 Dec 2024 10:37:57 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] rust: block: fix use of BLK_MQ_F_SHOULD_MERGE

Upstream-Commit: 31d813a3b8cbde2d09ba4dee282ca29096541006
Upstream-Repository: https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux.git
License: GPL-2.0-only

`BLK_MQ_F_SHOULD_MERGE` was removed from the C block API and merging is
now in effect by default. Remove the stale flag from Rust block-driver
tag sets. The exact Rocky 10.2 header has the new C semantics but its
Rust source retained the old flag reference, so generated bindings
correctly omit the symbol and Rust 1.92 reports E0425.

Link: https://lore.kernel.org/r/20241219060214.1928848-1-hch@kernel.org
Fixes: 9377b95cda73 ("block: remove BLK_MQ_F_SHOULD_MERGE")
Signed-off-by: Andreas Hindborg <a.hindborg@kernel.org>
[ Adapted the adjacent context to exact Rocky 6.12's `core::ffi::c_void`
  spelling; the upstream one-line semantic change is unchanged. ]
---
 rust/kernel/block/mq/tag_set.rs | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/rust/kernel/block/mq/tag_set.rs b/rust/kernel/block/mq/tag_set.rs
index f9a1ca6..338b21e 100644
--- a/rust/kernel/block/mq/tag_set.rs
+++ b/rust/kernel/block/mq/tag_set.rs
@@ -52,7 +52,7 @@ impl<T: Operations> TagSet<T> {
                     numa_node: bindings::NUMA_NO_NODE,
                     queue_depth: num_tags,
                     cmd_size,
-                    flags: bindings::BLK_MQ_F_SHOULD_MERGE,
+                    flags: 0,
                     driver_data: core::ptr::null_mut::<core::ffi::c_void>(),
                     nr_maps: num_maps,
                     ..tag_set
